class:: RoomDF
summary:: Dragonfly room reverb UGen
categories:: UGens>Effects
related:: Guides/DragonFlyReverb, Classes/EarlyReflectionsDF, Classes/HallDF, Classes/PlateDF

Description::

Native SuperCollider port of Michael Willis's Dragonfly Room Reverb. This UGen combines Dragonfly's Freeverb3 `earlyref` path with the scaled-down `progenitor2` late-reverb model to simulate smaller, tighter acoustic spaces. It accurately preserves the C++ DSP structure and parameter mapping of the original VST3 plugin without requiring a host environment.

While code::HallDF:: uses the massive `zrev2` delay network, code::RoomDF:: uses the `progenitor2` network. This network features a faster buildup of reflection density and a tighter overall delay scale. It is ideal for placing sounds in realistic studio rooms, vocal booths, and small performance spaces where the excessive modulation and long, blooming tails of a concert hall would be out of place.

classmethods::

method::ar

argument::inL
Left input.

argument::inR
Right input.

argument::dry
Dry level in percent (`0..100`). Controls the volume of the unaffected input signal.

argument::early
Early-reflection level in percent (`0..100`). Controls the volume of the initial geometric echoes.

argument::earlySend
Early-to-late send in percent (`0..100`). Controls how much of the early reflection energy is fed into the late reverberation tail generator.

argument::late
Late-reverb level in percent (`0..100`). Controls the volume of the dense reverberation tail.

argument::size
Size in meters (`8..32`). Affects the overall scale of the room. Smaller values sound like a tight booth, while larger values sound like a small live room.

argument::width
Stereo width in percent (`50..150`). Widens or narrows the stereo spread of the reverb.

argument::predelay
Predelay in milliseconds (`0..100`). The delay before the late reverb starts.

argument::decay
Decay time in seconds (`0.1..10`). The time it takes for the late reverb tail to fade to silence (RT60).

argument::diffuse
Diffusion in percent (`0..100`). Controls the smearing of reflections. High diffusion sounds smooth; low diffusion reveals individual echoes.

argument::spin
Modulation spin in Hz (`0..5`). The rate of chorus-like modulation inside the reverberation network. Usually kept low for realistic rooms.

argument::wander
Modulation wander in percent (`0..100`). The depth of the internal modulation.

argument::inHighCut
Input high cut frequency in Hz (`1000..16000`). Low-pass filter applied to the input signal before it enters the reverb generator.

argument::earlyDamp
Early damping frequency in Hz (`1000..16000`). Simulates the high-frequency absorption of the walls specifically for the early reflections.

argument::lateDamp
Late damping frequency in Hz (`1000..16000`). Simulates the high-frequency absorption of the walls and air for the late reverberation tail, causing higher frequencies to decay faster.

argument::boost
Low boost in percent (`0..100`). Amplifies low frequencies in the reverb tail, simulating the boomy resonance characteristic of many small enclosed rooms.

argument::boostLPF
Boost frequency in Hz (`50..1050`). The cutoff frequency below which the `boost` is applied.

argument::inLowCut
Input low cut frequency in Hz (`0..200`). High-pass filter applied to the input to prevent low-end rumble from cluttering the reverb.

Examples::

code::
(
{
	// Synthetic snare
	var src = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.01, 0.2), Impulse.ar(1)) * 0.5;
	
	// Synthetic high-bpm hi-hat:
	// var src = HPF.ar(WhiteNoise.ar, 8000) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.05), Impulse.ar(8)) * 0.5;
	
	// For live input instead:
	// var src = SoundIn.ar(0);
	
	RoomDF.ar(
		inL: src,
		inR: src,
		dry: 80.0,
		early: 40.0,
		late: 40.0,
		size: 15.0,
		decay: 0.8,
		diffuse: 80.0
	);
}.play;
)
::
